LiveKit is an open source platform for real-time voice, video and AI
agent applications. This package provides the LiveKit server, a
scalable, distributed WebRTC SFU (Selective Forwarding Unit) built on
Pion WebRTC that routes audio, video and data between participants.

Features include JWT-based authentication, simulcast and SVC, an
embedded TURN server, webhooks, a Twirp/HTTP room service API, and
multi-node operation coordinated through Redis, which is also used to
dispatch jobs to the separate LiveKit Egress and Ingress services.
